  <section class="process-section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-label" style="text-align:center;">How it works</div>
      <h2 class="section-h2">From First Consultation to Settled Life in Spain</h2>
      <p class="section-sub">Five steps, fully managed online, in plain English from start to finish.</p>

      <div class="process-steps">

        <div class="process-step">
          <div class="process-step__num">1</div>
          <div class="process-step__content">
            <h3>Eligibility Check &amp; Consultation</h3>
            <p>Start with our free online eligibility check — it takes under five minutes and confirms which visa route suits your situation: income level, employment type, nationality, and plans in Spain. For more complex situations, book a one-to-one consultation with a specialist who will review your specific circumstances and give you a clear, honest assessment of your options.</p>
            <div class="process-step__detail"><strong>Outcome:</strong> You know which visa is right for you, what the requirements are, and whether any complications need addressing before you start.</div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="process-step">
          <div class="process-step__num">2</div>
          <div class="process-step__content">
            <h3>Document Preparation &amp; Checklist</h3>
            <p>Once you engage the service, your case manager sends you a personalised document checklist tailored to your visa type, nationality, and chosen consulate. We don't send generic lists — every checklist reflects the specific requirements of your consulate (Edinburgh has different requirements from London; Miami differs from Los Angeles). As you gather documents, you upload them to your secure portal and we review each one before submission.</p>
            <div class="process-step__detail"><strong>Outcome:</strong> A fully reviewed, consulate-specific document pack — with every certificate, translation, and apostille confirmed correct before your appointment.</div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="process-step">
          <div class="process-step__num">3</div>
          <div class="process-step__content">
            <h3>Application Preparation &amp; Consulate Support</h3>
            <p>We prepare the complete application: all Spanish government forms, covering letters, financial summary documents, and any specialist documentation your case requires (employer letters, explanation letters for criminal record disclosures, school acceptance letters for children, investment income summaries). We book your consulate appointment where this is part of our service and brief you fully on what to expect at the interview.</p>
            <div class="process-step__detail"><strong>Outcome:</strong> A complete, professionally prepared application pack — ready to submit with confidence at your consulate appointment.</div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="process-step">
          <div class="process-step__num">4</div>
          <div class="process-step__content">
            <h3>Consulate Appointment &amp; Approval</h3>
            <p>You attend your consulate appointment with your completed application pack. We brief you in advance on the appointment format, likely questions, and what to bring. After your appointment, the consulate reviews your application — typically 4–10 weeks depending on the consulate and time of year. We monitor your application status and inform you when a decision is issued. For DNV applicants, we submit the Beckham Law application alongside the main visa where applicable.</p>
            <div class="process-step__detail"><strong>Outcome:</strong> Visa approval notification and your visa sticker issued in your passport — authorising you to enter Spain and live there legally.</div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="process-step">
          <div class="process-step__num">5</div>
          <div class="process-step__content">
            <h3>Post-Arrival Support &amp; TIE Card</h3>
            <p>Arriving in Spain is the beginning of a new phase, not the end of the process. Within 30 days of arrival you must complete several administrative steps: registering on the padrón (empadronamiento), applying for your TIE card at the Extranjería, and obtaining your NIE if not already done. We guide you through each of these steps and support you with TIE renewals, permanent residency applications, and the citizenship pathway in the years ahead.</p>
            <div class="process-step__detail"><strong>Outcome:</strong> Legal residency established in Spain, TIE card obtained, and a long-term support relationship in place for your entire journey — from arrival to citizenship if that is your goal.</div>
          </div>
        </div>

      </div>
    </div>
  </section>


